      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-161828",
      ":question/problem": "Let $f:U\\to R$ be continuously differentiable on an open set $U\u2286R$ such that $f(a)=b$ and ${f}^{\u2032}(a)\\ne 0$ for $a\\in U.$ Which of the following statements **must** be true?\n\n- The function $f$ is invertible on $U.$\n- The inverse ${f}^{-1}$ is continuously differentiable in a neighborhood of $b.$\n- The derivative of ${f}^{-1}$ is given by ${({f}^{-1})}^{\u2032}(b)=-{f}^{\u2032}(a).$"
    },
